=== F0. Sh_Phi o d = Rarita-Schwinger operator ===
  *^-1 Sh_Phi(xi ^ zeta)_a = lam * gamma_a gamma^b gamma^c xi_b zeta_c (b, c, a distinct) exactly, lam = +1: True   (random integer xi, zeta)

=== F1. Chirality ===
  Sh_Phi : maps Lambda^2 (x) S^+- into Lambda^13 (x) S^-+ (flips chirality): True; preserves chirality: False
  Sh_Phi': maps Lambda^2 (x) S^+- into Lambda^13 (x) S^-+ (flips chirality): True; preserves chirality: False
  Sh_gam : maps Lambda^2 (x) S^+- into Lambda^13 (x) S^-+ (flips chirality): True; preserves chirality: False
  d_0 = d + spin connection (Clifford grade 2, even) preserves chirality.  In row zeta-bar_- of (9.16) the entry
  *Sh(d_0 + w_{+-}) acts on zeta_- and the entry d_0 + w_{+-} on nu_-: outputs S^+ and S^- respectively, which no
  single invariant pairing with zeta-bar_- accepts (B, B' and the dual pairing are chirality-homogeneous).
  rank of [Sh_Phi(xi) | Sh_gam(xi)] on sample S^+-valued 2-forms (exact): 2  (2 => independent)

